---
title: Polenta Chips
source: https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2016/nov/10/how-to-make-the-perfect-polenta-chips
servings: 4
course: Side
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
---

Line a small baking dish with baking paper. Pour the @chicken or vegetable stock{650%ml} into a medium pan, add @polenta (coarse cornmeal){125%g}, bring to a simmer and then whisk until smooth. Simmer, stirring all the time, until it thickens and starts to come away from the side of the pan.

Stir in the @parmesan{50%g}(finely grated) until melted, then add the @chives{3%tbsp}(finely chopped) and pour into the baking dish, smoothing it into a flat layer about 1.5cm thick. Allow to cool completely, and then chill until solid.

Cut the polenta into chips and lightly coat with the remaining @polenta (coarse cornmeal){50%g}.

Cover the bottom of a #frying pan{} with @olive oil{}, and put it over a medium-high heat. Fry the chips in batches until golden brown on all sides, then drain on kitchen paper and keep warm in the oven until all the polenta is used up. Serve hot.